svx: chart data helpers a kit client can drive

ChartHelper gains IsChartData, SetChartData and WriteChartData: a
chart's own table under "data" as categories and series values. A
ragged table, or a value that is not a number or null, is refused. A
missing point reads and writes as null (the chart's own not-a-number
marker). An XY chart's categories are its X values: they must be
numbers and go in as numbers, not text. An XY chart whose series share
one X list reads with X as categories, from the series roles, as a
PPTX import has it; series with their own X lists are not one table and
the read leaves "data" out. The trailing attachData is gone: each
setter applies itself, and attachData put numbers back as text.

